# Archived release v1.0. The concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21731939 always
# resolves to the latest version.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21731939
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Target firmware, acquisition script and analysis code for a non-profiling
  correlation power analysis of the Shadow lightweight block cipher. All traces
  were acquired on a ChipWhisperer-Nano capture board with its on-board
  STM32F030F4 target, clocked at 7.5 MHz with one sample per clock cycle and
  firmware built at optimisation level -O0. The code covers Shadow-32 with a
  fixed key, Shadow-32 with ten independently chosen keys, and Shadow-64,
  together with a fixed-versus-random t-test of two masked Shadow-32
  implementations. The power traces it analyses are archived separately; see
  the related identifier below.
keywords:
  - side-channel analysis
  - correlation power analysis
  - lightweight block cipher
  - Shadow
  - masking
  - leakage assessment
references:
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Power traces for "Practical Key Recovery on the Shadow Lightweight Block
      Cipher with Non-Profiling Correlation Power Analysis"
